# Survey PDF Intelligence Platform — Full Production Pipeline (Kaggle)

End-to-end OCR pipeline converting scanned multi-page Hindi/English municipal
household survey PDFs into verified canonical JSON + CSV outputs, with a
Bayesian fail-closed evidence gate (`S >= 0.88` auto-accept, else
escalate to Hindi VLM, English OCR, IndicOCR, or template-prior override).

**GPU Required:** Settings → Accelerator → GPU T4 x2

---

## Inputs

| Dataset | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `rk9098/ward42-surveys` | 1446 Ward-42 survey PDFs |
| `rk9098/ocr-platform-code` | Pipeline source code (see setup below) |

## Outputs (in `/kaggle/working/output/`)

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ocr_results.csv` | Flat CSV — one row per family member |
| `evidence.db` | SQLite with cell-level provenance |
| `documents/*.json` | Per-PDF canonical JSON |
| `run_manifest.json` | Run metadata |

## Code dataset setup

If the `ocr-platform-code` dataset isn't available yet, run Cell 0 first to
recreate it from the notebook, then add it as an input.

Expected runtime: ~2–4 hours on T4 for 1446 PDFs.
